        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-17T19:18:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking closer at the spec, this state should be PE_VCS_CBL_Send_Soft_Reset and should be guarded by CONFIG_USBC_VCONN.\nWe could enter this state for any protocol errors send on SOP\u0027/SOP\u0027\u0027.  For this particular dock, we would send soft reset after getting no response from DiscSVID SOP\u0027.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 419,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 419,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "e1279fab25ae43512be11fff0e2dc05c8eb28204",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "887a5238_0274fe7c",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 419,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-17T20:31:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it considered a protocol error to not get a response for DiscSVID? PE_INIT_VDM_SVIDs_Request State doesn\u0027t list a soft reset on timeout.  There are a fair number of states written to just return to ready when they fail to get a response. \n\nI was thinking it probably wouldn\u0027t hurt to queue up a Soft Reset for the cable on startup generally.  I have a few docks and monitors that do this already.",
      "parentUuid": "850eca1e_22153bdb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 419,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 419,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "e1279fab25ae43512be11fff0e2dc05c8eb28204",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "98173ad9_7d7bb3db",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 419,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-18T00:10:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re correct - a response timeout doesn\u0027t appear to be a protocol error\n\nI\u0027ve seen monitors automatically issue soft resets on connect as well.  I\u0027ll have to check what the monitor does in the cause of a non-emarked cable to see how it manages retries.\n\nFor the dock in the linked bug, SOP\u0027 soft reset does seem to fix it.  It\u0027s unusual to issue DiscID first, then soft reset, but there\u0027s nothing the in spec to prevent this.  What do you think of this as a policy, or should we work towards always doing an SOP\u0027 soft reset before sending anything to the cable?",
      "parentUuid": "887a5238_0274fe7c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 419,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 419,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "e1279fab25ae43512be11fff0e2dc05c8eb28204",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f73606d1_0dff0bfd",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 419,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-21T16:23:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I lean towards doing the SOP\u0027 soft reset only from the READY states to avoid potential buggy paths our explicit contract negotiation, but I could be persuaded otherwise.  I think most peripherals I\u0027ve seen which soft reset do so before initial cable probing.\n\nI\u0027ve seen at least one monitor do this soft reset at startup poorly (ex. if Soft Reset process doesn\u0027t work, they forget to send Source Caps and the contract negotiation falls apart), so if we go that route I want to make sure we\u0027re coding it very robustly.  If we go the ready route, since we\u0027ve split our DiscoverIdentity retries over startup and ready, then we can at least ensure we\u0027ve tried the soft reset before our discover identity counter is reached and given the partner a fair shot.",
      "parentUuid": "98173ad9_7d7bb3db",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 419,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 419,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "e1279fab25ae43512be11fff0e2dc05c8eb28204",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "54f36304_ca0b7e19",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1739,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-17T17:30:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we alternatively have a DPM request to soft reset the cable which takes priority over discovery?  That would serve my own selfish purposes for b/152058087 (which you are welcome to take, should you feel so inspired :) )",
      "revId": "e1279fab25ae43512be11fff0e2dc05c8eb28204",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
